  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "accuracy",
    "affected_api": "numpy/_core/src/common/simd/neon/math.h npyv_sqrt_f32",
    "observed_behavior": "On ARMv7/armhf 32-bit platforms, the NEON SIMD sqrt path passes positive infinity (and zero) into vrsqrteq_f32, raising invalid floating-point errors; test_unary_spurious_fpexception[...-f-sqrt] fails with 'Got warnings' from warnings.WarningMessage objects.",
    "expected_behavior": "sqrt of positive infinity and zero should not raise spurious invalid floating-point errors; the guard substitutes 1.0 for zero and infinity inputs before the reciprocal-sqrt estimate so no invalid fp error is raised.",
    "manifestation": "warning",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "ARMv7 / armhf 32-bit platform (32-bit compatibility mode)",
      "sqrt operation on float32 input equal to positive infinity or zero",
      "test_unary_spurious_fpexception with f-sqrt data cases"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [],
    "oracle_clues": [
      "AssertionError: Got warnings: [<warnings.WarningMessage object ...>] in test_umath.py TestSpecialFloats::test_unary_spurious_fpexception[data16..19-escape16..19-f-sqrt]",
      "commit message: Fix floating-point errors with positive infinity input in sqrt on armhf",
      "the fix replaces guard_byz = vbslq_f32(is_zero, pinf, a) with vbslq_f32(is_special, one, a)",
      "no numeric expected/buggy output values given in passages; the oracle is absence of floating-point warnings during the test"
    ]
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": "float32",
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": null,
    "tolerance": null,
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "The sqrt fix in numpy/_core/src/common/simd/neon/math.h uses vrsqrteq_f32 on float32 (npyv_f32) lanes, and the guard was changed so positive infinity and zero inputs are replaced with 1.0f before the reciprocal-sqrt estimate, to avoid invalid floating-point errors on ARMv7/armhf.",
      "The return path was changed to vbslq_f32(is_special, a, sqrt), returning the input for zero and positive infinity inputs.",
      "The linspace denormal test test_denormal_numbers is marked xfail on armhf/AArch32 because those platforms appear to flush subnormals to zero even without FPSCR enabling FTZ.",
      "Passages from issue #24548 show selectedrealkind mismatches for real(16) kinds (e.g., selectedrealkind(16) returned -1 instead of 10, and selectedrealkind(32) returned -1 instead of 16), but these concern Fortran kind selection and are not the armhf sqrt bug itself."
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "Behavior depends on 32-bit ARM hard-float (armhf/AArch32 compatibility mode) and FTZ subnormal handling, which the passages do not quantify.",
      "The passages give no numeric tolerance or magnitude threshold at which correct and incorrect results separate.",
      "Issue #24548 kind-selection failures are a separate symptom and should not be conflated with the float32 sqrt infinity fix."
    ]
  },
